  "name": "Question 12",
  "problem": "The coefficient of ${u}^{3}$ in the expansion of ${(1-u)}^{20}$ is{{field-1}}.",
  "worked_solution": "The binomial expansion for $(1+x)^{n}$ is given by\n\n$$\n(1+x)^{n}=1+nx+\\frac{n(n-1)}{2!}{x}^{2}+\u22ef.\n$$\n\nIn particular, the ${x}^{3}$ term is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{n(n-1)(n-2)}{3!}{x}^{3}.\n$$\n\nReplacing $x$ with $-u$ and $n$ with $20$ in the above expression, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{20(20-1)(20-2)}{3!}\\cdot (-u)^{3} & =\\frac{20\\cdot 19\\cdot 18}{6}\\cdot (-u)^{3} \\\\  & =1140\\cdot (-{u}^{3}) \\\\  & =-1140{u}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coefficient of ${u}^{3}$ is $-1140.$",
